To keep the package small, some files are stored recompressed or in a
different file format (e.g. Stata .dta saved as .rds), and some contain only
the parts the package reads: the Mass Mobilization, SCAD, and Gapminder files
keep only the columns used; SIPRI keeps only the "Constant (2024) US$" and
"Share of GDP" sheets of its workbook, in long format; RAQED keeps only the
"Event table" sheet of its workbook; OMG omits its free-text note, source,
and coder columns; the ARC 2.0 events file omits its country name and
abbreviation columns; and NAVCO 3.0 keeps only the columns the package reads
(the event descriptions, source titles, actor names, and coder notes are
omitted). No values have been altered.

See the data-sources vignette for source URLs, versions, and citations. Anyone
redistributing the package is responsible for verifying that the applicable
third-party terms permit redistribution.
